## Drawer / sheet close — X only (no grabber)

**Golden sentence:** Studio drawers and bottom sheets **never** paint a top drag handle / grabber / "touch handlebar." Close is the **X** in the header (plus scrim / Escape where wired).

```
<dialog / sheet>
  <header>          ← title + X only
  <body>            ← content
```

| Do | Don't |
| --- | --- |
| Title + X close in the header row | `h-1 w-10 rounded-full` grabber above the header |
| Reuse `MOBILE_SHEET_HEADER` + `MOBILE_SHEET_CLOSE` (or chat settings twins) | Decorative `::before` / `aria-hidden` pill "handle" |
| Scrim / Escape as secondary dismiss | Grabber as the primary close signal |

**Forbidden:** touch handlebar node (`SHELL_CHAT_SETTINGS_HANDLE`, `mx-auto mt-2 h-1 w-10 rounded-full`); CSS grabber pseudo; Vaul-style drag pill with no real drag. **Not this rule:** pane **resize** handles (`SHELL_RESIZE_HANDLE`) — splitters, not drawer dismiss chrome.

