## Tab underline — no layout shift

**Golden sentence:** Underline / bottom-indicator tabs **always** reserve the indicator thickness — idle = transparent (or matching track), active = brand. Switching tabs must **not** change row height or shove content. Section tab strips also leave **clear air below** the track.

| State | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Idle | `TAB_UNDERLINE` — `border-b-2 border-b-transparent` (sides/top 0) |
| Active | `TAB_UNDERLINE_ACTIVE` — same width, `border-b-brand-600` |
| Section strip | `SECTION_TABS` / `SECTION_TAB` / `SECTION_TAB_ACTIVE` |

```ts
// ✅ same geometry both states — color only
class={active ? ui.SHELL_RAIL_TREE_TAB_ACTIVE : ui.SHELL_RAIL_TREE_TAB}
// ❌ width only on active
class={active ? "border-b-2 border-brand-600" : "border-b-0"}
```

| Do | Don't |
| --- | --- |
| Always `border-b-2` (or fixed `h-*` underline via `::after` / inset shadow) on **every** tab | Idle with no bottom border / `border-b-0` |
| Idle `border-b-transparent`; active brand | Toggle border **width** between states |
| `box-border`; keep font-weight / padding identical across states | Pair `border-0` with `border-b-2` — shorthand can zero the reserved edge |

### Below the strip (section tabs)

| Relationship | Min gap | Tailwind | Token |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Window chrome → tab track | **12px** | `pt-3` on strip | `space.3` |
| Tab track → first content section | **12px** | `mb-3` on strip (or `pt-3` on content) | `space.3` |
| Comfort / dense chrome | 16px | `mb-4` / `pt-4` | `space.4` |

Keep gap on the **strip or the content start** — one owner. Rail/dock underlines that sit flush in a chrome band don't force `mb-3` — only **section strips**. Alternatives (also no-shift): `::after` absolute bar, inset `box-shadow`, or full-row track `border-b` + active overlay.

